## Fixed Issues
  #XXXX - TRoE: fixed the postgres connection-pool wedge ("no connection to postgres" + "Internal Error (bug in postgres connection pool logic?)" for every DB operation until a broker restart). Root cause was twofold. (1) The pool had no wait mechanism: queueSem was created as a free-slot counter (init = poolSize) but pgConnectionGet posted it right back on every path and pgConnectionRelease never posted it - so with all slots borrowed, the next caller did not queue but fell through both search loops and failed instantly (reproduced against a healthy postgres: 16 threads on a 4-slot pool -> 480 of 640 gets returned NULL). (2) Nothing bounded how long a slot stays borrowed: no connect_timeout (a blackholed TCP connect blocks ~2 min x 30 attempts with the slot already busy), no TCP-keepalive tuning (kernel default: first probe after 2 h), no statement_timeout - a thread stuck inside libpq held its slot forever, and once poolSize threads were stuck the pool was wedged permanently. Now: pgConnectionGet waits (EINTR-safe sem_timedwait, 10 s) for a free slot, and on timeout logs every slot's state incl. the postgres backend PID (findable in pg_stat_activity); pgConnectionRelease posts the free-slot unit back, rolls back a transaction left open on the connection (previously it poisoned the next borrower - every statement failed with "current transaction is aborted") and PQfinishes dead connections (previously the PGconn leaked its socket - as it also did in the two places where pgConnectionGet freed a dead slot without PQfinish); connections are created with connect_timeout=5, TCP keepalives (idle 30s/interval 10s/count 3) and statement_timeout + idle_in_transaction_session_timeout (new CLI option -troeStmtTimeout / env TROE_STMT_TIMEOUT, default 60000 ms, 0 = disabled), so stuck queries and dead peers self-heal in bounded time instead of holding slots forever; the pool list is mutex-protected (two threads first using the same tenant could create duplicate pools / a torn linked list); pgTransactionBegin/Commit check the SQL result status (a COMMIT answered with ROLLBACK - aborted transaction - or a non-idle transaction status after COMMIT is now a failure, so the Kafka path NACKs instead of committing the offset for a non-durable batch); fixed a pool-slot leak plus NULL dereference in pgDatabasePrepare's error path (cfrey-de - Carsten Frey)
  #XXXX - Kafka ingest: the consumer committed the Kafka offset right after the MongoDB upsert but BEFORE the TRoE (temporal/Postgres) write. A TRoE failure (Postgres down, connection drop, SQL error) therefore lost the temporal instance permanently - MongoDB kept the newer value, the history did not, and the offset was already gone so the batch was never redelivered. The offset is now committed only after BOTH the MongoDB upsert and the TRoE write succeed. pgCommands() now flags failures in orionldState.troeError (and additionally catches SQL-level command failures via PQresultStatus - previously only a dead connection or a NULL result was detected); a flagged batch is left uncommitted so Kafka redelivers it (cfrey-de - Carsten Frey)
  #1943 - Fixed crash on a malformed q-filter with a missing AND/OR separator between two expressions (e.g. q=category=="office"category!="inactive" - missing ';'): qLexCheck did not validate the token following a String/Boolean/Integer/Float value, so the malformed token stream reached qParse and triggered a NULL dereference. Such input is now rejected with 400 Bad Request
  #1899 - Fixed broker startup stall on a cyclic @context in the persisted context cache: at startup the cached @contexts are reloaded, and an array-@context re-downloads its referenced contexts recursively. A context that references itself (directly or via a chain) made the loader wait the full download timeout (3s) per cycle in contextCacheWait - which exists to let one thread wait for ANOTHER thread already downloading the same context, but during the single-threaded startup recursion the "other downloader" is the same thread, so the wait could never be satisfied (and with enough cross-referencing contexts the cumulative stall trips orchestrator startup probes -> CrashLoop). The recursion now detects same-thread re-entry and rejects the cyclic @context immediately. Such non-fatal context-load failures are now logged as warnings instead of errors, so they no longer look like a failed startup
  #XXXX - Batch delete (non-legacy path): a duplicated Entity ID is now handled per NGSI-LD spec clause 10.3.6 - the first occurrence is deleted and each subsequent occurrence gets a ResourceNotFound (404) error in the 207 response (the duplicates were previously dropped silently)
  #1951 - Fixed slow, half-broken batch upsert of more than 1000 entities: the legacy "which of these already exist" lookup (mongoCppLegacyEntityListLookupWithIdTypeCreDate) truncated its result at a hardcoded 1000, so on a re-upsert the surplus entities were misclassified as new and re-inserted (duplicate-key path) instead of updated. The lookup's $in query is already bounded by the batch (and thus by the max payload size), so the arbitrary 1000 cap was removed
  #1943 - Fixed heap corruption / crash under concurrent load: the MHD request thread pool (enabled by reqPoolSize, recently turned on by default) runs MHD in epoll mode, multiplexing several connections onto each pool thread - but the in-progress request state (payload buffer, kalloc, requestTree) lives in the thread-local orionldState, so concurrent (large, multi-chunk) requests corrupted each other (heap use-after-free / "free(): invalid size"). The MHD thread pool is now disabled: the broker always runs thread-per-connection. The -reqPoolSize/TRQ_POOL_SIZE option is still accepted (so existing deployments start) but is ignored and logs a warning
  #XXXX - Fixed entity corruption from PATCH /entities/{id}/attrs carrying a body datasetId: the datasetId instance was moved aside but never written, and the emptied attribute clobbered the stored default instance (the next read 500'd). PATCH /attrs does not implement datasetId instances - it is now rejected with 501 and the entity is left untouched
  #XXXX - Fixed stale value in notifications when PATCH /entities/{id} (merge) updates an EXISTING datasetId instance: the notification render only folded the patched dataset instances in when the attribute had no instances in the DB yet, so an update notified the old DB value (and a DDS action's terminal notification dropped its ddsActionResult entirely). The patched instances are now merged into the render entity in all cases
  #1905 - TRoE: segfault (exit 139) connecting to TimescaleDB Cloud - added SSL support and fixed NULL pointer crash
  #XXXX - Fixed crash under concurrent notification delivery by replacing thread-unsafe gethostbyname with getaddrinfo in orionldServerConnect
  #XXXX - Fixed query of many large entities (cfreyfh - Carsten Freyh at Fraunhofer IKTS)
  #XXXX - Wait for postgres instead of exiting after the first try - just like for mongo (1 try per second during 30 secs)
  #XXXX - Fixed crash in relationship endpoint when no relations found (cfreyfh)
  #XXXX - Fixed crash in GET /types when entity has empty attrNames (NULL attr name from MongoDB aggregation)
  #XXXX - Fixed crash in POST /entityOperations/query when entities array contains non-object items
  #XXXX - Fixed crash in batch update when entity payload contains "scope" field
  #XXXX - Fixed crash in PATCH entity when entity doesn't exist locally but distOps are active
  #XXXX - Fixed crash in TRoE for POST /entities with distOps returning 207 (requestTree was NULL)
  #XXXX - Fixed TRoE crash on POST /temporal/entities with NULL requestTree
  #XXXX - Fixed hang on POST /temporal/entities when using -mongocOnly (legacy mongoEntityExists blocked on semaphore)
  #XXXX - Fixed duplicate key error log for context cache persistence (ignore already-persisted contexts)
  #XXXX - Fixed default MQTT port not set when URI has no explicit port (now defaults to 1883/8883)
  #XXXX - Fixed "scope" not skipped in distOpResponses success attribute list
  #XXXX - Fixed Location header for POST /jsonldContexts to use relative path (per ETSI API spec)
  #XXXX - Fixed crash in pernot notification with simplified format (NULL serviceP dereference)
  #XXXX - Fixed Ngsild-Attribute-Format header in pernot notifications (was hardcoded to Normalized)
